m":234,"icon":235},"Grind Jobs","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fgrind-jobs","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F02.grind-jobs","i-lucide-workflow",{"title":237,"path":238,"stem":239,"icon":174},"Project Publishing Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fproject-publishing-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F03.project-publishing-design",{"title":241,"path":242,"stem":243,"icon":33},"Sign-In Design","\u002Fplatform\u002Freference\u002Fsign-in-design","04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F04.sign-in-design",{"title":245,"path":246,"stem":247,"icon":248},"Development Server","\u002Fplatform\u002Fdevelopment-server","04.platform\u002F13.development-server","i-lucide-server-cog",{"title":250,"path":251,"stem":252,"icon":253},"Supply Chain Security","\u002Fplatform\u002Fsupply-chain-security","04.platform\u002F14.supply-chain-security","i-lucide-package-check",{"title":255,"path":256,"stem":257,"icon":258},"Enterprise License","\u002Fplatform\u002Fenterprise-license","04.platform\u002F15.enterprise-license","i-lucide-badge-check",{"id":260,"title":227,"body":261,"description":1233,"extension":1234,"links":1235,"meta":1236,"navigation":1237,"path":228,"seo":1238,"stem":229,"__hash__":1239},"docs\u002F04.platform\u002F12.reference\u002F01.cri-format.md",{"type":262,"value":263,"toc":1216},"minimark",[264,268,272,276,287,294,298,308,314,318,323,326,365,369,376,383,389,393,400,455,461,471,484,548,551,619,622,626,629,635,639,642,648,652,655,661,665,672,912,916,922,1123,1127,1212],[265,266,26],"h2",{"id":267},"overview",[269,270,271],"p",{},"A CRI (Kinotic Resource Identifier) is used by Kinotic to route requests to the appropriate service, method, or event stream. It is a URI-like format with parts named for clarity within the Kinotic platform.",[265,273,275],{"id":274},"format","Format",[277,278,283],"pre",{"className":279,"code":281,"language":282},[280],"language-text","scheme:\u002F\u002F[scope@][zone~]resourceName[\u002Fpath][#version]\n","text",[284,285,281],"code",{"__ignoreMap":286},"",[269,288,289,290,293],{},"Everything in brackets (",[284,291,292],{},"[]",") is optional.",[265,295,297],{"id":296},"case","Case",[269,299,300,301,304,305,307],{},"Every part keeps the case it was written with, and addresses match by exact string comparison — ",[284,302,303],{},"OrderService"," and ",[284,306,303],{}," are two different addresses. Service names carry the case of the class that published them, so a typical address looks like:",[277,309,312],{"className":310,"code":311,"language":282},[280],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~org.kinotic.management.api.services.ProjectService\u002FfindByRepoFullName\n",[284,313,311],{"__ignoreMap":286},[265,315,317],{"id":316},"components","Components",[319,320,322],"h3",{"id":321},"scheme","Scheme",[269,324,325],{},"Identifies the type of resource being addressed.",[327,328,329,341],"table",{},[330,331,332],"thead",{},[333,334,335,338],"tr",{},[336,337,322],"th",{},[336,339,340],{},"Description",[342,343,344,355],"tbody",{},[333,345,346,352],{},[347,348,349],"td",{},[284,350,351],{},"srv",[347,353,354],{},"Published services and their methods",[333,356,357,362],{},[347,358,359],{},[284,360,361],{},"stream",[347,363,364],{},"Event streams (not yet routable through the gateway)",[319,366,368],{"id":367},"scope","Scope",[269,370,371,372,375],{},"An optional qualifier that narrows the CRI to a specific context, such as a tenant ID, user ID, or device ID. When present, it appears before the ",[284,373,374],{},"@"," symbol.",[269,377,378,379,382],{},"If a scope needs sub-scopes, use the format ",[284,380,381],{},"scope:sub-scope",".",[277,384,387],{"className":385,"code":386,"language":282},[280],"srv:\u002F\u002Ftenant-123@app.acme-org.orders-app~OrderService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fdevice-42@app.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[284,388,386],{"__ignoreMap":286},[319,390,392],{"id":391},"zone","Zone",[269,394,395,396,399],{},"The optional zone places the resource in the isolation boundary the gateway validates on every send and subscribe. It precedes the resourceName, separated by ",[284,397,398],{},"~",". A zone is one or more dot-separated labels of lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[327,401,402,410],{},[330,403,404],{},[333,405,406,408],{},[336,407,392],{},[336,409,340],{},[342,411,412,425,435,445],{},[333,413,414,419],{},[347,415,416],{},[284,417,418],{},"app.\u003CorganizationId>.\u003CapplicationId>",[347,420,421,422,382],{},"One application's services. Only that application's participants and the owning organization's runtimes can call them, through the app server, the one server that reaches these zones; they are hosted by the owning organization's runtime, which authenticates as an organization participant. Applications may nest their own sub-zones, e.g. ",[284,423,424],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app.billing",[333,426,427,432],{},[347,428,429],{},[284,430,431],{},"app-api",[347,433,434],{},"The platform's data plane for applications, such as entity persistence and named query execution. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[333,436,437,442],{},[347,438,439],{},[284,440,441],{},"management-api",[347,443,444],{},"The platform services organizations manage the system through, such as member, application, and entity definition management. Hosted in-process by the platform only.",[333,446,447,452],{},[347,448,449],{},[284,450,451],{},"system-api",[347,453,454],{},"The system's own services. Only system participants can call or host them.",[269,456,457,458,460],{},"A cluster member outside the platform's servers can host its services in ",[284,459,441],{},", where organizations' users call them through the management server as they call the platform's own; such a service checks the caller's organization itself.",[269,462,463,464,467,468,470],{},"Organization and application ids become zone labels, but only ever after the ",[284,465,466],{},"app"," prefix, so they cannot collide with the platform's own zones. The one exception is guarded explicitly: creating an organization or application whose name slugifies to ",[284,469,451],{}," is rejected.",[269,472,473,474,476,477,480,481,483],{},"Which zones a connection may address is determined by the authenticated participant. A participant may also address any sub-zone of a zone it is allowed, so ",[284,475,424],{}," is reachable by whoever may reach ",[284,478,479],{},"app.acme-org.orders-app",". An address without a ",[284,482,398],{}," carries no zone at all and is only reachable by system participants.",[327,485,486,499],{},[330,487,488],{},[333,489,490,493,496],{},[336,491,492],{},"Participant",[336,494,495],{},"May send to",[336,497,498],{},"May subscribe to",[342,500,501,517,536],{},[333,502,503,506,514],{},[347,504,505],{},"APPLICATION (org, app)",[347,507,508,510,511],{},[284,509,431],{},", ",[284,512,513],{},"app.\u003Corg>.\u003Capp>",[347,515,516],{},"reply destinations only",[333,518,519,522,531],{},[347,520,521],{},"ORGANIZATION (org)",[347,523,524,510,526,510,528],{},[284,525,441],{},[284,527,431],{},[284,529,530],{},"app.\u003Corg>.*",[347,532,533,535],{},[284,534,530],{}," — its applications' zones",[333,537,538,541,544],{},[347,539,540],{},"SYSTEM",[347,542,543],{},"everything",[347,545,546],{},[284,547,451],{},[269,549,550],{},"Each server also has a zone partitioning, the zones it hosts and the zones it reaches. A node advertises a service\nto the cluster only in a zone its server hosts, and sends only to zones its server reaches: an address in any\nother zone has no handlers there. An address without a zone passes both.",[327,552,553,566],{},[330,554,555],{},[333,556,557,560,563],{},[336,558,559],{},"Server",[336,561,562],{},"Hosts",[336,564,565],{},"Reaches",[342,567,568,585,602],{},[333,569,570,573,577],{},[347,571,572],{},"org",[347,574,575],{},[284,576,441],{},[347,578,579,510,581,510,583],{},[284,580,441],{},[284,582,451],{},[284,584,431],{},[333,586,587,590,596],{},[347,588,589],{},"system",[347,591,592,510,594],{},[284,593,451],{},[284,595,441],{},[347,597,598,510,600],{},[284,599,451],{},[284,601,441],{},[333,603,604,606,613],{},[347,605,466],{},[347,607,608,510,610],{},[284,609,431],{},[284,611,612],{},"app.*",[347,614,615,510,617],{},[284,616,431],{},[284,618,612],{},[269,620,621],{},"The gateway applies the partitioning before a frame reaches the event bus: a send to a zone the server does not\nreach, or a subscription in a zone it does not host, is refused whatever the participant may address. The\nservice directory and listener monitors still see every registration in the cluster, so a service hosted by one\nserver shows as online from any other, while each server's MCP listing shows only the tools in zones it reaches.",[319,623,625],{"id":624},"resource-name","Resource Name",[269,627,628],{},"The name of the resource being addressed, excluding the zone. For services, this is the fully qualified service name. For streams, this is the event type name.",[277,630,633],{"className":631,"code":632,"language":282},[280],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\n",[284,634,632],{"__ignoreMap":286},[319,636,638],{"id":637},"path","Path",[269,640,641],{},"An optional path that identifies a specific part of the resource, such as a method name on a service. The path's case is preserved.",[277,643,646],{"className":644,"code":645,"language":282},[280],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById\nstream:\u002F\u002Fapp.acme-org.orders-app~temperature\u002Fsensor-1\n",[284,647,645],{"__ignoreMap":286},[319,649,651],{"id":650},"version","Version",[269,653,654],{},"An optional semantic version for the resource. Enables versioned service routing so multiple versions of a service can coexist.",[277,656,659],{"className":657,"code":658,"language":282},[280],"srv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService\u002FfindById#1.0.0\nsrv:\u002F\u002Fmanagement-api~com.example.UserService#2.0.0